    <section class="empire-glance" id="at-a-glance" aria-labelledby="glance-title">
      <div class="empire-glance-main"><h2 class="empire-glance-title" id="glance-title">At a glance</h2><ul><li>A Tai kingdom founded in 1228 by Sukaphaa that ruled the Brahmaputra valley of Assam for six centuries.</li><li>The paik system made every free adult man owe labour or military service, supporting roads, embankments and armies.</li><li>The Ahoms resisted the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#mughal-empire">Mughal Empire</a>, winning at Saraighat in 1671, before rebellion and Burmese invasions ended the state.</li></ul></div>
      <aside class="empire-dyk"><p class="empire-dyk-title">Did you know?</p><p>Ahom kings were buried in earthen mounds called maidams at Charaideo, which <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia#unesco-world-heritage-site">UNESCO</a> inscribed as a World Heritage Site in 2024.</p></aside>
    </section>

